      },
      "message": "fix(sim): simulate a stock held in a vise; model quarter-turned stock\n\nA locate that did not turn the part wrote the solve's float noise\n(about 5e-14) into the following stock's rotation. The stock sim and\nthe viewport's traced stock refused each non-identity rotation, so the\nstock in a vise was not simulated and the refusal was said twice.\n\n- MoveModel keeps the stock's own rotation when the move does not turn\n  the part.\n- stock_follow::sim_frame is the one law for the sim's stock frame: a\n  box or upright cylinder turned by a quarter-turn multiple is its\n  unturned twin; a from-model stock reads its placed mesh; an oblique\n  box or a laid cylinder is refused in plain words. stock_grid,\n  first_body, first_field and the field view read it.\n- The UI says a simulation refusal once, in plain words, and the uncut\n  stock stays drawn.\n\nFixes #2177\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
