      "message": "test(sim): keep the not-judged device off the quarter turn\n\nThe program sim now judges a stock turned a quarter about Z (#2177).\nFour suites used that turn to make the sim refuse, so that the\noperation's own gouge was the only judge of the post. Their nine by_op\nchecks saw the sim's gouge clause first.\n\nThe device is now a turn of 1e-6 rad about Z, which the sim refuses by\nname (OBLIQUE_STOCK); each by_op check asserts that refusal too. Each\nsuite gets a test that the quarter-turned stock is judged, its gouge\nblocks the post, and a legal mark posts. The MCP parity test of\nstock_source_law moves to stock_source_law_mcp (400-line law).\n\nRefs #2177\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
